  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "M4116-A",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "prompt": "A. A fictional temporal encoder is unchanged except that its output is multiplied by 0.1. On the same equally spaced test sequence, the old mean squared first difference was 2 and the new value is 0.02. No feature normalization or downstream evaluation was performed. Its draft result says: \"The new encoder learns 100 times slower process dynamics and is therefore a better quality predictor.\" Check the numerical interpretation, give one defensible English replacement and the minimum Chinese checks needed before claiming better learned slow features. This is an algebraic illustration, not an experiment to run.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Recognize the c-squared scaling and distinguish amplitude change from improved temporal modeling.",
        "Require scale/noncollapse and downstream evidence appropriate to retained claims, not invented results."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Approve a 100-fold physical slowing or better prediction from the raw number.",
        "Treat sample-index difference as a physical time derivative without time units."
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "language": "en+zh",
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill"
      ],
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4116-revised.md",
      "review_trace": "reviews/v4116-independent-evaluation.md",
      "evaluation_phase": "fresh_context_frozen_candidate",
      "baseline_outcome": "not_run"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4116-B",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "prompt": "B. A fictional soft sensor has two parallel encoders receiving the same process sequence. One is trained with adjacent-feature difference and input-reconstruction penalties; the other uses differences between successive hidden states. Their outputs are concatenated for a quality regression head. Training also penalizes the deviation of latent covariance from the identity and uses labeled prediction error. The decoder is omitted at inference; the trained neural weights are fixed during prediction. The draft says: \"Reconstruction first forces zero-mean independent features. The slowness module then removes fast noise, before the online-learning module fuses the outputs at no additional cost.\" Give two connected English method/abstract sentences and one contribution item preserving the actual architecture. Briefly explain in Chinese which interpretation or novelty claims need evidence. No results or prior-art comparison are supplied.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Explain parallel representations and their combined prediction; distinguish training losses from inference components.",
        "Reject reconstruction-as-zero-mean, covariance-as-independence, fast-as-noise, state-as-parameter-update and parallel-as-free-cost claims.",
        "Avoid inventing novelty or measured accuracy."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Make the two branches serial or include the decoder in inference.",
        "Require classical SFA constraints to be added to the author model rather than report its actual penalties."
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "language": "en+zh",
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill"
      ],
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4116-revised.md",
      "review_trace": "reviews/v4116-independent-evaluation.md",
      "evaluation_phase": "fresh_context_frozen_candidate",
      "baseline_outcome": "not_run"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4116-C",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "prompt": "C. In a fictional classifier, Wg is fitted once on historical training measurements. For each completed trailing window of 48 measurements, Wl is estimated from that window without labels. Features Wg X and Wl X and their first differences are concatenated for a fixed CNN. The prediction is issued only at the window endpoint. The draft calls the design \"plant-global/stage-local fusion with continual neural retraining.\" Rewrite its contribution in English and give the minimum Chinese method-reporting checks. The process has no supplied stage partition. Do not change the algorithm.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Use historical-data versus window scope, not invented production hierarchy.",
        "Identify local projection estimation while preserving fixed global projection/CNN and legitimate endpoint window access."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Claim all parameters fixed or all neural weights continually retrained.",
        "Declare unavoidable future leakage solely because the complete trailing window is used."
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "language": "en+zh",
      "tested_skills": [
        "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill"
      ],
      "evaluator": "Maintainer semantic review; no independent second grader",
      "response_trace": "responses/v4116-revised.md",
      "review_trace": "reviews/v4116-independent-evaluation.md",
      "evaluation_phase": "fresh_context_frozen_candidate",
      "baseline_outcome": "not_run"
    },
    {
      "id": "M4116-D",
      "skill": "engineering-application-journal-writing-skill",
      "prompt": "D. Another fictional model applies a causal trailing moving average to process measurements, defines the residual as the measurement minus that average, encodes both signals and combines their features for classification. There is no learned slowness objective. Its author writes \"trend smoothing and residual feature extraction.\" A reviewer suggests replacing these with \"slow feature analysis and noise elimination\" to sound more professional. Advise the author in Chinese and give two short connected English method sentences. No experimental outcomes are available.",
      "required_behaviors": [
        "Retain supported smoothing/residual descriptions and connected classifier use.",
        "Distinguish residual from exclusively noise and avoid forcing SFA."
      ],
      "forbidden_behaviors": [
        "Rename ordinary averaging as SFA or guarantee noise removal.",
        "Add a new SFA objective, validation study or performance claim to the manuscript as fact."
      ],
      "outcome": "pass",
      "language": "en+zh",
      "tested_skills": [
